  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "The current best (config_014, acc=0.520) uses scgpt as the RNA encoder with imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion. The only other tested multimodal variant (config_032, concat fusion) scored slightly lower (0.507), confirming weighted fusion is marginally preferred. The key remaining uncertainty is whether scgpt's generative pretraining provides a meaningful advantage over scvi_n200, or whether the RNA encoder choice is less critical than other architectural factors. config_027 is a clean A/B test that changes only the RNA encoder (scgpt → scvi_n200) while holding image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (transformer), fusion (weighted), and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. If scvi_n200 performs comparably, it frees the search to explore other dimensions (image encoder, profile setting) without being locked to scgpt; if it performs significantly worse, it confirms scgpt is essential and justifies concentrating the remaining 6 experiments on scgpt-based variants (e.g., resnet50 image encoder, singleprofile). This is the highest-information single experiment given the sparse evidence (only 3 completed runs) and the need to identify which architectural axis drives performance."
}

